WEBVTT

01:00.260 --> 01:01.320
Here she comes.

02:42.870 --> 02:46.350
I'd like you to come 
to the College, Chise.

02:54.110 --> 02:57.890
I believe I've spoken about it before.

02:58.800 --> 03:02.790
You mentioned that it's a school for 
sorcerers and a mutual aid organization.

03:02.790 --> 03:04.140
I'm not convinced.

03:05.200 --> 03:09.000
Why should Chise go to such
 a place, when she is a mage?

03:10.940 --> 03:14.910
In addition to being a Sleigh Beggy,

03:14.910 --> 03:17.470
Chise carries two curses with her.

03:17.470 --> 03:20.160
The curse of the dragon, 
and the curse of immortality.

03:20.940 --> 03:23.630
I apologize if this comes
 across as insensitive,

03:23.630 --> 03:27.130
but as a researcher, she's too 
great an opportunity to pass up.

03:29.490 --> 03:31.820
Might we ask for your cooperation?

03:32.370 --> 03:35.830
Of course, we would support you to 
the best of our ability, as well.

03:36.230 --> 03:41.860
If you'd like, we can arrange for you to 
take classes with the other students.

03:43.260 --> 03:45.350
We won't burden you overmuch,

03:45.350 --> 03:48.220
and I'll ensure you receive the maximum 
compensation we can offer.

03:49.280 --> 03:52.610
Maybe we'll even find 
a way to lift the curses.

03:58.200 --> 03:58.920
Chise.

04:01.590 --> 04:04.330
I'll step out for the time being.

04:04.330 --> 04:05.520
Please, talk it out.

04:11.400 --> 04:14.180
What do you think, Elias?

04:14.180 --> 04:15.940
I absolutely hate it.

04:16.550 --> 04:19.060
I don't want them prodding at you.

04:20.800 --> 04:21.750
But...

04:23.150 --> 04:24.280
What about you?

04:29.050 --> 04:31.930
I've been thinking for a while now...

04:33.590 --> 04:37.520
About how I don't know anything.

04:38.200 --> 04:45.910
It's why I default to sacrificing 
myself whenever there's a need.

04:47.340 --> 04:50.450
Even though people tell 
me that's a bad thing.

04:51.530 --> 04:54.550
I told you not to try to do
 everything by yourself.

04:54.550 --> 04:59.190
You think that by destroying yourself, 
you can earn the right to be here.

05:00.560 --> 05:04.060
I don't understand why that's bad.

05:04.060 --> 05:08.060
What's the difference between 
what you tried to earn

05:08.060 --> 05:11.410
by sacrificing yourself, and what I want?!

05:13.010 --> 05:16.190
But if there are things I can learn

05:16.190 --> 05:19.030
in order not to have to sacrifice 
myself to solve problems...

05:20.340 --> 05:24.390
If I can accomplish what I want 
without hurting anyone...

05:25.140 --> 05:26.680
I want to learn that.

05:27.010 --> 05:32.510
It might be of help to me 
or someone else someday.

05:39.160 --> 05:41.060
They might dissect you.

05:41.540 --> 05:45.680
You'll help me if they try, right?

05:46.770 --> 05:49.000
I understand your point of view.

05:50.580 --> 05:53.090
I have a lot to say, but, well...

05:53.700 --> 05:58.460
I'll attend the College with you, then.

05:59.000 --> 05:59.740
Huh?

06:04.000 --> 06:08.280
Pleased to meet you. I'm Liza.

06:09.890 --> 06:12.040
Liza Quillyn.

06:12.040 --> 06:14.760
I'm the president of the English College.

06:15.210 --> 06:19.090
Thank you sincerely for your 
cooperation, Chise Hatori.

06:19.090 --> 06:22.270
We intend to repay you properly.

06:24.980 --> 06:26.210
Here you are.

06:26.210 --> 06:27.560
As a token of welcome.

06:31.630 --> 06:33.580
Thank you.

06:33.580 --> 06:39.590
This place exists to protect and nurture 
not just you, but everyone here.

06:41.050 --> 06:46.040
Try not to become too complacent, but make 
yourself at home and enjoy your time here.

06:46.630 --> 06:47.510
Okay.

06:49.020 --> 06:50.760
Good day.

06:52.820 --> 06:56.180
As of today, you'll be 
a special student here.

06:56.180 --> 07:00.010
Ainsworth will be a visiting 
instructor in the Magic Department.

07:00.430 --> 07:02.480
I'll take you there next.

07:05.850 --> 07:07.330
How was she?

07:09.310 --> 07:10.950
Promising.

07:10.950 --> 07:14.690
She may be a bit lacking in confidence, 
but she seems to have a strong will.

07:15.290 --> 07:16.870
Meaning?

07:18.580 --> 07:22.600
She steers her own ship.

07:26.110 --> 07:28.330
A sky underground?

07:28.330 --> 07:31.750
We're using sorcery to project 
the sky from another location.

07:31.750 --> 07:33.330
Now, this way, please.

07:39.010 --> 07:41.450
This is a view of the entire College.

07:41.920 --> 07:45.030
It's comprised of several 
underground towers.

07:51.060 --> 07:53.180
The administration tower 
is here in the center.

07:53.180 --> 07:54.370
The training tower,

07:54.370 --> 07:55.900
book management tower,

07:55.900 --> 07:57.210
dormitory tower,

07:57.210 --> 07:58.680
classroom tower,

07:58.680 --> 08:00.170
laboratory tower,

08:00.170 --> 08:03.750
and waste disposal facility
 tower, making seven in total.

08:03.750 --> 08:07.630
Each tower then is separated 
into different floors.

08:08.950 --> 08:12.390
You don't have to remember all of this now.

08:12.670 --> 08:14.190
Uh-huh...

08:14.990 --> 08:20.970
Now, I'd like to show you around 
each of the towers right away...

08:20.970 --> 08:27.510
But, there's someone waiting eagerly 
to meet you first. My apologies.

08:28.470 --> 08:29.970
Welcome!

08:30.510 --> 08:32.480
Th-Thanks.

08:34.310 --> 08:37.360
I'm Alexandra Heath.

08:37.720 --> 08:40.430
I'm in charge of the medical room.

08:41.170 --> 08:42.720
Chise Hatori.

08:43.260 --> 08:45.190
Follow me.

08:45.190 --> 08:47.650
We'll get your examination 
done in the other room.

08:47.650 --> 08:49.610
You won't have to worry 
about any prying eyes.

08:52.830 --> 08:55.370
No observers, please.

08:56.380 --> 08:58.780
I'm her guardian.

09:00.150 --> 09:03.380
There are things that are difficult 
to say, especially to friends,

09:03.380 --> 09:06.800
especially to family, and 
especially to guardians.

09:08.920 --> 09:10.670
U-Um...

09:10.670 --> 09:12.230
I'm sorry.

09:12.230 --> 09:18.480
I still haven't finished giving these 
two a tour of the College yet.

09:18.480 --> 09:19.580
So...

09:25.070 --> 09:27.740
Then you two have fun together!

09:31.700 --> 09:35.450
Well... I'll show you around 
the staff room, then.

09:36.090 --> 09:37.710
I don't need a room.

09:42.000 --> 09:43.580
I see.

09:43.580 --> 09:46.760
You made a fairy medicine and nearly died.

09:46.760 --> 09:50.290
You took in a dragon's 
curse and nearly died.

09:50.290 --> 09:54.420
You were gutted by a wandering 
sorcerer and nearly died.

09:54.420 --> 09:58.680
And then you swapped eyeballs and 
were given his curse of immortality.

10:01.450 --> 10:02.740
Quite the troublemaker, hmm?

10:05.520 --> 10:10.100
You seem quite reckless, 
but you've done well.

10:11.320 --> 10:14.480
You must think about the people 
around you, too, though.

10:16.060 --> 10:17.120
Yes.

10:17.570 --> 10:20.920
Well, is there anything else 
that you'd like to discuss?

10:24.370 --> 10:25.400
Actually...

10:29.600 --> 10:32.640
I was a little surprised earlier.

10:34.880 --> 10:36.530
In the medical room, I mean.

10:37.490 --> 10:42.530
I thought you might refuse 
to leave her side.

10:42.530 --> 10:45.660
I mean, you can hide in 
the shadows, can't you?

10:48.160 --> 10:52.570
I don't have any biological 
organs inside my body.

10:55.230 --> 11:00.920
Yet, when I think about the time 
Chise caught me hiding near her...

11:01.710 --> 11:04.990
I feel something like my organs tensing.

11:06.870 --> 11:08.350
So I won't do it.

11:10.350 --> 11:12.350
You mean, you're afraid?

11:13.060 --> 11:14.280
Afraid?

11:14.280 --> 11:16.140
Oh, um...

11:16.140 --> 11:21.030
I'm just saying I might personally describe 
that as the sensation of being afraid.

11:23.430 --> 11:24.590
Afraid...

11:25.010 --> 11:26.320
I see.

11:27.470 --> 11:31.000
It's not a sensation I'd like 
to experience for too long.

11:33.020 --> 11:35.520
Why did you come to the College with her?

11:36.090 --> 11:37.390
What changed?

11:38.040 --> 11:39.900
I had no choice.

11:39.900 --> 11:41.590
You could say I'm here as a guard.

11:41.880 --> 11:43.230
I see.

11:45.420 --> 11:48.360
The Seven Shields are not a monolith.

11:49.390 --> 11:51.820
The current absence is significant.

11:51.820 --> 11:53.530
It's somewhat unstable.

11:54.140 --> 11:57.060
Please do keep a good eye on her.

11:57.490 --> 11:58.290
Right.

12:06.590 --> 12:08.150
<i>He's right, though.</i>

12:09.440 --> 12:15.700
<i>To think I'd be doing such a thing, 
in such a populous place...</i>

12:21.500 --> 12:24.520
<i>I wonder what she's doing right now.</i>

12:25.320 --> 12:28.660
<i>Would she be surprised if 
she learned about me now?</i>

12:29.840 --> 12:31.380
Ainsworth.

12:37.880 --> 12:41.060
Ever since you swapped left 
eyes with the sorcerer,

12:41.060 --> 12:45.600
you have frequent flashbacks 
to memories that aren't yours.

12:45.600 --> 12:49.420
And you've become sensitive to malice,
the gazes of others, and other presences.

12:51.970 --> 12:55.420
But you're feeling well
 otherwise, at least physically?

12:55.760 --> 12:59.030
If anything, I've been even better 
since the wound on my stomach healed.

12:59.560 --> 13:02.660
I can lift heavy things now.

13:02.660 --> 13:03.980
How heavy, specifically?

13:05.840 --> 13:09.510
<b></b>Yoink

13:06.580 --> 13:08.280
About two people's worth?

13:08.280 --> 13:09.520
Fantastic!

13:09.950 --> 13:14.300
How many years' worth of memories 
would you say you've seen?

13:20.070 --> 13:23.870
Not all of it is clear.

13:24.840 --> 13:27.700
But about a thousand years, I think.

13:28.320 --> 13:31.910
That's more than enough to 
dwarf your own awareness.

13:32.540 --> 13:35.330
Do people ever tell you that 
your personality's changed?

13:35.780 --> 13:41.390
Or do you ever consider options that you 
certainly never would have in the past?

13:41.990 --> 13:43.650
Not yet.

13:47.120 --> 13:47.800
Who's that?

13:55.720 --> 13:56.860
Chise?!

13:59.370 --> 14:00.740
I'm sorry.

14:01.620 --> 14:04.730
I felt like someone was watching me.

14:07.030 --> 14:09.100
No, it's all right.

14:09.100 --> 14:12.990
Let's just keep an eye on you for a while.

14:12.990 --> 14:13.660
Okay.

14:20.620 --> 14:22.970
This is the staff room.

14:24.300 --> 14:26.000
You're going to live here?

14:26.910 --> 14:29.110
No, I'm commuting.

14:29.110 --> 14:30.310
Commuting?

14:30.310 --> 14:32.260
It'd take at least three hours each way.

14:32.880 --> 14:34.890
I know a shortcut.

14:36.460 --> 14:38.280
Are you commuting, too?

14:38.280 --> 14:39.950
The same as us, then.

14:39.950 --> 14:41.610
I'm not the same as you.

14:43.260 --> 14:46.090
You hate me, don't you?

14:46.090 --> 14:48.520
Have I done something to you?

14:51.250 --> 14:54.080
You aren't the only one I hate.

15:00.220 --> 15:04.760
I'm sure his hatred isn't personal.

15:04.760 --> 15:08.540
He's been notoriously misanthropic 
since his student days.

15:09.140 --> 15:13.550
I'm certain I <i>am</i> hated, 
just not that intensely.

15:15.330 --> 15:19.570
I don't feel the need 
to kill him, after all.

15:25.630 --> 15:27.030
By the way...

15:27.660 --> 15:30.840
What exactly should I do for class?

15:31.270 --> 15:34.560
I figured you'd ask, so I brought a manual.

15:38.790 --> 15:41.570
I followed Alexandra's directions, but...

15:42.280 --> 15:44.570
Are these the dorms she was talking about?

15:45.020 --> 15:46.700
Don't ask me.

15:46.700 --> 15:49.860
She said there's dorm matron here.

15:49.860 --> 15:51.410
My, oh my!

15:52.080 --> 15:54.150
What a wonderful scent.

15:54.150 --> 15:56.630
An unusual smell.

15:57.250 --> 15:59.210
The smell of magic.

16:04.090 --> 16:05.120
Cats.

16:05.120 --> 16:07.300
I'm Olivia.

16:07.300 --> 16:08.280
Camellia.

16:08.280 --> 16:09.400
Rose Lyn.

16:09.400 --> 16:12.250
And our mother, Florence.

16:13.580 --> 16:15.040
<i>They're cats...</i>

16:15.040 --> 16:17.210
<i>But not the kind of cats I know.</i>

16:18.580 --> 16:20.220
You're the new girl.

16:20.220 --> 16:21.690
Do you know what grade you're in yet?

16:22.740 --> 16:24.120
Um...

16:24.120 --> 16:26.250
I'm a first-year in junior high school.

16:27.660 --> 16:28.810
Uh...

16:28.810 --> 16:31.230
Are you the dorm matrons?

16:31.230 --> 16:33.060
Yes, that's us.

16:35.300 --> 16:37.960
You can ask us anything you'd like.

16:37.960 --> 16:40.610
You can trust us with any of your worries.

16:40.610 --> 16:42.750
You can tell us anything you'd like.

16:42.750 --> 16:47.010
However, if you do any bad-mouthing, we'll 
scratch and bite you until you're crying.

16:47.890 --> 16:51.320
So, which of us would you like for your home?

16:53.880 --> 16:56.860
Oh, wait.

16:58.580 --> 17:00.190
This way.

17:01.010 --> 17:03.210
Over here.

17:05.040 --> 17:09.370
Here, you'll find children who love their 
homes, children who hate their homes,

17:09.370 --> 17:12.650
children who don't want their homes, 
children who have no homes...

17:12.650 --> 17:14.090
All kinds of children.

17:14.780 --> 17:18.270
We're here for the children who live here.

17:19.060 --> 17:23.230
If you're honest and proud 
of your history, choose Olivia.

17:23.610 --> 17:26.540
If you love the future and 
seek it out, choose Camellia.

17:27.630 --> 17:30.650
If you have freedom in your
 heart, choose Rose Lyn.

17:34.280 --> 17:36.750
Who do you want for your home?

17:40.390 --> 17:43.350
I already have a home, but...

17:44.740 --> 17:48.310
Someone once told me that I'm free.

17:52.080 --> 17:55.290
I leave myself in your care, Rose Lyn.

17:56.330 --> 17:59.020
Likewise, Hatori Chise.

17:59.400 --> 18:03.010
Stay out of trouble, child of Rose Lyn.

18:03.010 --> 18:04.430
Well, nice to meet you.

18:13.860 --> 18:15.860
This is your room here.

18:17.200 --> 18:22.650
You can read all the rules in 
the book in the desk drawer.

18:24.270 --> 18:27.220
Communicate well with your roommate.

18:27.220 --> 18:29.790
Don't hold back when you 
need to laugh or cry.

18:30.160 --> 18:33.090
And enjoy every day.

18:33.540 --> 18:34.920
Understood?

18:35.610 --> 18:36.430
Yes.

18:36.430 --> 18:39.140
Come to me if you ever need anything.

18:39.140 --> 18:41.020
Thank you.

18:48.970 --> 18:53.310
<i>I hope I won't be interrupting 
if someone's trying to sleep.</i>

18:53.860 --> 18:56.520
<i>Should I knock to avoid being rude?</i>

18:57.250 --> 18:59.910
<i>I don't want to wake them up, though...</i>

19:01.090 --> 19:03.420
<i>I'm getting nervous.</i>

19:05.790 --> 19:07.550
<i>She's creepy, right?</i>

19:07.990 --> 19:10.030
<i>She's always on her own.</i>

19:10.310 --> 19:12.290
<i>I've never seen her smile.</i>

19:12.760 --> 19:15.010
<i>I saw her talking to herself in class.</i>

19:15.010 --> 19:15.750
<i>Ew.</i>

19:20.070 --> 19:21.420
<i>No way.</i>

19:21.420 --> 19:23.810
<i>They're all sorcerers.</i>

19:23.810 --> 19:27.560
<i>I'm sure they'll understand me, 
even when I'm being weird...</i>

19:27.560 --> 19:30.490
<i>Wait, no, they might be suspicious of me.</i>

19:39.570 --> 19:42.790
Even Joseph wasn't this scary.

19:44.880 --> 19:45.970
<i>But...</i>

19:47.960 --> 19:51.240
<i>I'm here to seek things out.</i>

19:52.650 --> 19:53.250
Okay.

19:58.740 --> 20:02.010
Why didn't you knock?!

20:02.010 --> 20:03.440
I-I'm sorry!

20:03.440 --> 20:06.890
I didn't expect anyone to be right there.

20:07.270 --> 20:09.730
You were dawdling in front of the door!

20:09.730 --> 20:10.900
Of course I saw you!

20:10.900 --> 20:12.990
S-Sorry.

20:16.410 --> 20:18.700
Whatever, you're forgiven.

20:19.340 --> 20:21.730
You're my new roommate, aren't you?

20:25.360 --> 20:26.460
Lucy.

20:26.820 --> 20:28.600
Lucy Webster.

20:30.070 --> 20:31.950
Chise Hatori.

20:32.990 --> 20:34.740
Nice to meet you.

20:35.960 --> 20:37.840
Your bed's over there.

20:37.840 --> 20:38.870
That's your desk.

20:38.870 --> 20:41.130
The dorm rules are in the drawer.

20:41.130 --> 20:42.880
Your uniform's in the closet.

20:44.060 --> 20:44.470
Uh...

20:44.470 --> 20:45.260
Got it?

20:45.530 --> 20:46.380
Yes.

20:46.980 --> 20:51.320
Also, I'm not good at talking to people.

20:51.320 --> 20:54.780
If you want someone to 
chat with, find someone else.

20:54.780 --> 20:57.010
That'll make it easier for both of us.

20:57.640 --> 21:00.300
I'm gonna sleep until right 
before class starts.

21:00.540 --> 21:01.920
Don't wake me up.

21:19.490 --> 21:20.580
<i>It's okay.</i>

21:21.810 --> 21:23.690
<i>It's just been a while.</i>

21:24.260 --> 21:27.580
<i>Having a hole in my stomach was way worse.</i>

21:34.940 --> 21:35.940
<i>Okay.</i>

21:58.460 --> 22:01.060
Where's the training room?

22:01.060 --> 22:03.300
Again, don't ask me.

22:12.720 --> 22:13.640
Chise!

22:16.150 --> 22:18.160
What do I even do?

22:19.070 --> 22:21.030
I'm usually on the other 
side of this situation.

22:22.790 --> 22:24.280
I don't know what to do.
